.TH REBOOT 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
reboot \- restart the computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reboot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reboot
ends every process, closing their files (so what they wrote reaches the
disks), and restarts the computer: it goes off and on again, and the
EEPROM boots afresh. It takes no arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
It does not return when it works. If the kernel refuses, the reason is
printed and the status is 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR poweroff (1),
.BR halt (1)
